course: dictionary
lesson: 590
title: Autumn: the season of falling leaves
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Autumn is one of the four seasons of the year. It comes between summer and winter. Read «In autumn trees stop making green chlorophyll, so hidden yellows and oranges show through.» The clue is that autumn is a time when trees change, so it is a season of the year.
explain: The words around autumn can tell you when it happens. «Hedgehogs feed up in autumn, then hibernate in a nest of leaves» shows that autumn comes before the long winter sleep. Autumn is when days get shorter and cooler and leaves change colour and fall.
explain: In American English people often say fall for this season, so «fall» in a US book can mean autumn. When autumn comes before a word, as in autumn leaves or autumn colours, it describes that thing, just as a colour word would.
explain: The months depend on where you live. In the UK, Ireland, USA and Canada autumn is September to November. In Australia and New Zealand it is March to May, because their seasons are the other way round.
fact: Autumn is the season between summer and winter.
fact: In autumn the leaves change colour and fall, and the days get shorter and cooler.
fact: In American English this season is mostly called «fall».
fact: In autumn trees stop making green chlorophyll, so hidden yellows and oranges show through.
fact: In the UK, autumn term is the first term of the school year.
exercise: What does autumn mean? | A month in the middle of winter | The first day of spring | *The season between summer and winter | A kind of tree
exercise: In which months is autumn in the UK? | March to May | June to August | *September to November | December to February
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that is another name for autumn in American English: «In America, the trees look lovely in the fall.» | *fall | America | trees | lovely
test: Why do autumn leaves look yellow and orange? | *Because the green chlorophyll stops, so the hidden colours show through | Because the leaves are dead and dry | Because the wind paints them each morning | Because it is always sunny in autumn
test: Ayesha in Sydney says autumn starts in March. Is she right? | No, autumn is always in September | No, autumn is in June | *Yes, in Australia autumn is March to May | No, that is the start of winter
exam: Swallows leave Britain for warm Africa every ___ because there are almost no flying insects to eat in winter. | spring | *autumn | Christmas | Easter
